    "https://www.uvm.edu/human-resources/careers": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | Human Resources | The University of Vermont Skip to main content Human Resources University of Vermont Human Resources Search Close Search All UVM Search People Menu Close Menu Menu Human Resources Explore UVM Main navigation About Admissions Academics Research Campus Life Athletics Quick links My UVM Login to your UVM Dashboard GIVE TO UVM VISIT UVM Academic Calendar Bookstore Commencement Parking and Transportation Summer University UVM News Virtual Tour quick links Login to your UVM Dashboard GIVE TO UVM VISIT UVM Academic Calendar Bookstore Commencement Parking and Transportation Summer University UVM News Virtual Tour group nav Human Resources Home Careers Talent Development Total Rewards (Benefits and Compensation) Resources Employee Hiring and Management Retiree Forms Library (NetID required) Engagement Contact Us Contact Us Human Resources University of Vermont 85 South Prospect Street Burlington, VT 05405 Phone: +18026563150 hrinfo@uvm.edu Explore Payroll Office of Equal Opportunity Search Jobs UVM Foundation UVM Athletics Cultural Resource Guide Connect Instagram Linkedin Explore Human Resources Home Careers Talent Development Total Rewards (Benefits and Compensation) Resources Employee Hiring and Management Retiree Forms Library (NetID required) Engagement Contact Us hide menu Careers UVM Works For people and planet UVM is a premier research institute rooted in discovery, creativity, community, and action. Located in Burlington, we are known for our commitment to sustainability, diversity, and community impact. In a vibrant setting enriched by the surrounding natural landscapes, UVM emphasizes environmental leadership, experiential learning, and innovation, creating solutions that benefit Vermont and beyond. For you UVM is known for its award-winning Employee Wellness program, competitive and comprehensive benefits, and a commitment to your personal and professional growth. Find a job you love in a community where you and your family can thrive. Find a Job Whether you're looking to join the UVM family or are seeking a new opportunity as a current employee, find the right next step in your career and apply with our jobs portal. UVM Jobs Find a Job Whether you're looking to join the UVM family or are seeking a new opportunity as a current employee, find the right next step in your career and apply with our jobs portal. UVM Jobs Why UVM? A commitment to academic excellence, intellectual freedom, and making an impact is at the center of everything we do. This commitment is brought to life by the work of faculty and staff across a wide range of UVM colleges, departments, offices, centers, programs, and initiatives. Learn more about UVM UVM News A Totally Rewarding Experience UVM's Total Rewards package is comprised of health & welfare benefits, compensation, and the other perks that come with being a UVM employee. It is a key component to why so many employees come to - and stay at - UVM. Total Rewards Wellness in Work and Life UVM is committed to supporting the whole person by fostering a culture of wellbeing, offering flexible work options that adapt to your unique needs, and providing diverse opportunities for personal and professional growth. Employee Wellness Talent Development More ways to engage at UVM A Community Like No Other With a rich array of shared cultural, social, and community-focused resources and opportunities, UVM and Burlington celebrate collaboration, innovation, and shared purpose that lead to big impacts. Cultural Resource Guide Campus Events Values in Action At UVM, we believe in the transforming power of education and agree to help create and foster an environment where we can discover and reach our true potential. Our Common Ground Our Commitment to Sustainability Our Commitment to Inclusive Excellence Housing for UVM Staff and Faculty Body Catamount Run Apartments offer a unique, exclusive housing opportunity for UVM faculty and staff. Developed in partnership with the university, this brand-new community is ideally located in the heart of South Burlington’s City Center, just one mile from campus. Residents enjoy modern studio, one-, two-, and three-bedroom floor plans, along with convenient access to dining, shopping, and everyday essentials. UVM employees also receive complimentary public transportation through Green Mountain Transit , making commuting to and from campus simple and stress free. Our Commitment to Equal Opportunity and Access Body UVM is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity. We celebrate diversity and are dedicated to creating an equitable and accessible workplace. UVM does not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status in our hiring or employment practices. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance or accommodation due to a disability during the application or interview process, please contact hrinfo@uvm.edu or (802) 656-3150 Find our more about Accessibility and Accommodation at UVM Contact Human Resources 85 South Prospect Street 228 Waterman Building Burlington, VT 05405 hrinfo@uvm.edu (802) 656-3150 Explore Payroll Office of Equal Opportunity Search Jobs UVM Foundation UVM Athletics Cultural Resource Guide Connect Instagram Linkedin University of Vermont home Accessibility Privacy/Terms of Use"
    },
