      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Executive Assistant to the Dean Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Executive Assistant to the Dean Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Executive Assistant to the Dean Posting Summary The Executive Assistant to the Dean will provide comprehensive, executive and administrative support to the Dean of the College of Engineering and Mathematical Sciences ( CEMS ). Serve as a primary point of contact and coordination for the Dean by managing a complex calendar; screening, prioritizing, and routing requests. Prepare routine correspondence and materials. Coordinate and set up meetings, including scheduling, room reservations, technology needs, agendas, materials, records, and follow-up tracking. Support Dean’s Office leadership and Dean’s Office initiatives with administrative projects by organizing information, maintaining accurate files, and escalating issues that require leadership attention. Consistently exercise discretion and sound judgment when handling sensitive, confidential, and time-critical information and communications. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Associate’s degree in a related field and five (5) years of related experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Working knowledge of software applications used to support administrative operations and familiarity with internet resources and proficiency with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams) required. Demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple activities with attention to detail, meet deadlines, and maintain accurate records. Effective interpersonal, organizational, and written communication skills required. Demonstrated ability to exercise discretion and maintain confidentiality when working with sensitive information. Desirable Qualifications Experience providing executive-level administrative support in a complex office environment. Experience coordinating sensitive calendars, preparing briefing materials, managing confidential communications, tracking decisions and follow-up items. Familiarity with university processes. Anticipated Pay Range $26.50-$34.00/hr Other Information Final compensation will be determined in consideration of the finalist’s experience.. Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), This position is ineligible for telework due to the essential functions, Background Check required for this position FLSA Non-Exempt Union Position No Posting 