    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88106": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate/Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway - General Neurologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Assistant/Associate/Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway - General Neurologist Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy General Neurology Position Assistant/Associate/Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway Robert Larner, M.D. College of Medicine University of Vermont The Department of Neurological Sciences at the Robert Larner, M.D. College of Medicine ( LCOM ) in alliance with University of Vermont ( UVM ) Health seeks to recruit a physician to join our evolving program in General-Comprehensive Neurology. This is a full-time 1.0 FTE clinical position with a corresponding faculty appointment in the Department of Neurological Sciences at LCOM . All applicants must be Neurology Board eligible/certified. Fellowship training in a clinical neurology discipline is preferred but not required. This position provides clinical care to patients at UVM Health while engaging in the education of residents, fellows, and medical students. The successful candidate is expected to oversee the resident clinic at UVM Health and participate in the expansion of the department’s general neurology and neuro-hospitalist programs. We welcome applications from qualified candidates, including those who require work authorization sponsorship. UVM Health is located in Burlington, Vermont and serves the state as its only academic medical center. Burlington is a small but vibrant community on the shores of Lake Champlain between the Adirondack and Green Mountains. The area offers year-round recreational opportunities, safe communities, and excellent schools, while Burlington itself is frequently cited as among the most livable cities in the United States. The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground : Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through their teaching, service, research, scholarship, or creative arts. Successful candidates will exhibit a strong commitment to the tenets of Our Common Ground and the principles of professionalism . Applicants are requested to include in their cover letter information about how they will enhance the impact of Our Common Ground values and professionalism. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. Applicants must apply online at: www.uvmjobs.com under Position No. XX. Applications must include: · CV · Cover letter summarizing qualifications and how they will enhance the impact of Our Common Ground values and professionalism. · Contact information for three references Questions about this opportunity may be directed to: Waqar Waheed, MD, via email at Waqar.Waheed@uvmhealth.org . Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Employment is subject to a successful background check. Anticipated Pay Range Assistant Professor: $280,000-$320,000 Associate: $300,000-$330,000 Professor: $320,000-$350,000 Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/16/2025 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3492PO Department Neurological Sciences/55800 Advertising/Posting Title Assistant/Associate/Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway - General Neurologist FLSA Exempt Position Number 00027655 Employee FTE 1.0 Employee Term (months) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document (1) ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/87638": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy The Department of Nursing in the College of Nursing and Health Sciences ( CNHS ) at the University of Vermont ( UVM ) invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track position at the rank of clinical assistant/associate professor to serve as a clinical faculty member and Department of Nursing Director of Simulation Education. In addition to contributing to the teaching mission of the department, this position provides strategic, administrative, and faculty leadership for all simulation-based education within the Department of Nursing, including low-, medium-, and high-fidelity simulation. This is a 10-month appointment. Responsibilities Teach in the undergraduate and/or graduate Nursing programs Provide leadership for all nursing simulation activities. Design, implement, and evaluate simulation learning experiences aligned with curricular outcomes. Collaborate with nursing faculty on scenario design and standardized patient training. Serve as Department of Nursing representative on CSL Operations Team and Advisory Board. Support faculty development in simulation pedagogy across CNHS and interprofessional partners. Track simulation budgets and recommend new technologies and materials. Qualifications Doctorate in Nursing with an emphasis in simulation preferred (PhD or DNP ) Master of Science in Nursing ( MSN ) from an accredited nursing education program required Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator ( CHSE ) credential eligibility Current or eligible unencumbered license to practice as a Registered Nurse in the state of Vermont Demonstrated expertise in simulation education and debriefing methodologies Experience in teaching Nursing curriculum Minimum of five (5) years of recent clinical nursing experience in direct patient care At least two consistent years of focused implementation of simulation practices, to include design, mentorship and professional development participation Strong interest in innovation, emerging technologies, and faculty development The University Established in 1791, the University of Vermont is a nationally recognized public research university that combines the close faculty–student engagement of a liberal arts college with the resources of a comprehensive research institution. UVM is known for excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement, as well as a longstanding commitment to social justice, sustainability, and inclusive excellence. These values are embedded across academic programs and campus life and guide the University’s mission to prepare students to be thoughtful, engaged leaders in an increasingly complex and diverse world. The College of Nursing and Health Sciences The College of Nursing and Health Sciences serves approximately 1,200 students across undergraduate and graduate programs and is deeply committed to interprofessional education, clinical excellence, and educational innovation. The College brings together multiple health professions in a collaborative academic environment that prepares graduates to work effectively in team-based, patient-centered care settings. CNHS emphasizes experiential learning, simulation-based education, community engagement, and the integration of emerging technologies to prepare students for the evolving healthcare landscape. The Department The successful candidate will join a dynamic and supportive Department of Nursing committed to excellence in clinical teaching, student mentorship, and innovative nursing education. The Department includes approximately 40 full-time and 40 part-time clinical faculty who work collaboratively to educate a vibrant and diverse student body of more than 500 undergraduate students and over 100 graduate students. Academic offerings include an undergraduate Bachelor of Science in Nursing, a Direct Entry Master’s program, and a Doctor of Nursing Practice ( DNP ) program, including a direct entry option. Check our website for more information: www.uvm.edu/ and www.uvm.edu/~cnhs/nursing. The Community The University of Vermont is located in Burlington, Vermont, consistently ranked as one of the best small cities in the United States. Set on the shores of Lake Champlain between the Green Mountains and the Adirondacks, Burlington offers a vibrant mix of natural beauty, cultural life, and community engagement. The area is known for its commitment to sustainability and social justice, year-round outdoor recreation, and a welcoming, close-knit community, making it an exceptional place to live and work.. Application Process The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Applicants are required to submit a statement reflecting their commitment to advancing these values. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to legally protected status. Applications should be submitted online at www.uvmjobs.com/87636 . Application materials should include 1) a cover letter and statement of interest, 2) CV, 3) statement reflecting commitment to advancing Our Common Ground Values. Additional Required Information Effective Date of Appointment: August 24, 2026 Appointment Length: 10-month, non-tenure track clinical faculty appointment Rank/Title: Clinical faculty rank and title will be commensurate with education and experience Applicants must provide a minimum of three professional references. These references should collectively reflect the candidate’s performance in both academic and clinical settings. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check Salary: Compensation or salary range will be disclosed in accordance with Vermont law Anticipated Pay Range $80,236 – $96,000 Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 03/06/2026 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3633PO Department Nursing/56010 Advertising/Posting Title Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing FLSA Exempt Position Number 00025953 Employee FTE 1.0 Employee Term (months) 10 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document (1) Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/87439": {
      "title": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Davis Center Facilities Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Davis Center Facilities Manager Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Davis Center Facilities Manager Posting Summary Provide leadership, direction, and oversight for facilities of the Dudley H. Davis Center, a 200,000 square foot student union and conference center. Coordinate services with various campus partners including Physical Plant, Grounds, Facilities Design & Construction, and Custodial Services, as well as external contractors. Oversee daily facilities functions. Recommend and oversee building maintenance, repairs, and renovation projects, ensuring compliance with UVM and Davis Center standards and safety measures. Assist with developing facilities budgets and monitor expenditures. Manage building furniture and equipment, and coordinate purchasing, repair, and disposal. Coordinate with the Business Manager and Associate Director to create short term and long-term plans for equipment replacement and building renewal. Oversee building tenant relationships, addressing needs and space concerns. Participate in developing, maintaining, and communicating emergency preparedness plans and policies. Supervise facilities staff. Operate with a high degree of independence in managing daily facility needs while supporting strategic priorities established by departmental leadership. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Associate’s degree and five years related work experience including demonstrated experience in facility management, student unions, or hospitality management. Experience with construction projects. Demonstrated supervisory experience. Basic computing skills including Microsoft Office Suite and Microsoft Teams. Valid driver’s license or ability to obtain a driver’s license required. Desirable Qualifications Knowledge/experience with construction/ renovation. Familiarity with collective bargaining. Understanding of room scheduling software. Knowledge of Microsoft Office software suite. Anticipated Pay Range $60,000 - $65,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position No Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 07/24/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Fac Mgmt & Services PC3 X Posting Number S6234PO Department Davis Center Ops & Events/11590 Position Number 00024017 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) * Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
