    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/86975": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate/Professor - Inpatient Psychiatry Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Assistant/Associate/Professor - Inpatient Psychiatry Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy Faculty Position – Inpatient Psychiatry Service The University of Vermont, Robert Larner, MD, College of Medicine and the University of Vermont Medical Center ( UVMMC ) are seeking a full-time faculty member at the Assistant/Associate/Professor level on the clinical scholar pathway to join an enthusiastic team of professionals on the Inpatient Psychiatry Service. This 28- bed state-of-the-art adult unit located in a 400-bed university-based general hospital is a principal teaching site for residents and medical students. This attending psychiatrist will join an existing inpatient team of psychiatrists, nurses, social workers, activities therapists, and psychologists to provide psychiatry inpatient care at the UVM Medical Center in Burlington. The candidate will provide direct patient care and team leadership on two units in a busy tertiary hospital. The University of Vermont, Robert Larner, MD, College of Medicine Psychiatry Service hosts medical students on clerkships and electives, sponsors a residency in psychiatry, and sponsors a fellowship in child psychiatry. This faculty member will be a key participant in the education of trainees at several levels. The selected candidate will demonstrate the training and expertise to provide direct patient care, collaborate with other professional disciplines, and work with referring agencies and providers. In addition, the candidate will be responsible for supervision and teaching of house officers, medical students, and other staff. An appreciation of the importance of and satisfaction from performing these critical functions and an ability to work collaboratively are essential. Applicants must have a medical degree and be board certified (preferably) or board eligible in psychiatry. Interest and experience in inpatient psychiatry is very desirable. Qualified applicants are invited to apply online, with CV and cover letter at www.uvmjobs.com Burlington, Vermont is located in the beautiful Lake Champlain region, surrounded by the Green and Adirondack Mountains. It is a great place for families, boasting excellent schools and year-round recreational opportunities. It is home to the University of Vermont and many other colleges that provide an academically stimulating and culturally rich environment. Montreal and Boston are within easy driving distances. The University is especially interested in candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community through their research, teaching, and/or service. Applicants are requested to include in their cover letter information about how they will further this goal. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. The University encourages applications from all individuals who will contribute to the diversity and excellence of the institution. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. If you have any questions about this position, please contact: Sanchit Maruti, MD Email: Sanchit.Maruti@uvmhealth.org Anticipated Pay Range Job Location Job Open Date 02/01/2023 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F2545PO Department Psychiatry/55750 Advertising/Posting Title Assistant/Associate/Professor - Inpatient Psychiatry FLSA Exempt Position Number 00024121 Employee FTE 1.0 Employee Term (months) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88219": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President for Economic Development",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Associate Vice President for Economic Development Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Associate Vice President for Economic Development Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Associate Vice President for Economic Development Posting Summary We will begin reviewing applications as of 10/15/2026 Reporting to the Vice President for Research and Economic Development ( VPR ), the Associate Vice President ( AVP ) for Economic Development provides strategic leadership for statewide economic development, industry engagement, workforce solutions, innovation, partnerships, and entrepreneurship. The AVP also serves as a senior integrator and primary connector among university offices and resources and external partners, translating institutional strengths into mutually beneficial partnerships and new initiatives with measurable economic and public impact. Strategic Innovation and Leadership The AVP is responsible for identifying, developing, launching and evaluating strategic initiatives that advance the university’s economic and innovation priorities, in alignment with the strategic direction of the VPR and in coordination with relevant university units. The AVP will leverage institutional strengths and emerging opportunities to create partnerships and programs that generate measurable economic, research, community, workforce, and financial impact. The AVP will: Cultivate and sustain executive-level relationships with corporations, state and local government agencies, entrepreneurs, investors, business associations, chambers, economic development agencies, nonprofit organizations, and community leaders. In partnership with the Office of Engagement, lead discovery with prospective partners to understand their research, innovation, talent, workforce, commercialization, or community needs and connect them with the appropriate UVM expertise and resources and where appropriate, help develop opportunities into actionable initiatives by defining the value proposition, partners, resource requirements, and measures of success. Develop and advance strategic and deep partnerships that may combine sponsored research, entrepreneurship support, workforce development, talent recruitment, internships, technology licensing, testing and validation, philanthropic engagement, and new venture creation. Coordinate with the UVM Foundation Corporate Relations Office, Vermont Center for Emerging Technologies, and other relevant university and external partners to present a unified approach and clarify ownership and advance opportunities efficiently. Represent UVM in regional and statewide economic development strategy discussions and help position the university as a trusted convener and implementation partner. Managerial Role The AVP provides strategic leadership of and coordinates economic development activities and strategic initiatives under the leadership of the VPR . As a portfolio leader and manager, the AVP will: Provide direct leadership for five units within OVPR , including UVM Innovations, Office of Engagement, Leahy Institute for Rural Partnerships, Biolabs Innovation Hub, and the Vermont Gallium Nitride Technology Hub. In coordination with each unit’s leader, identify, prioritize, and advance new and/or stronger economic development activities, such as corporate partnerships, support for entrepreneurs, and revenue-generating activities like research partnerships, fee-for-service programs, and UVM -connected start-up businesses. Coordinate economic development activities with the UVM Foundation Corporate Relations Office and the Vermont Center for Emerging Technologies, and other units within the University as needed. Oversee and guide unit leaders to ensure their work aligns with organizational goals and missions and that units participate in strategic initiatives, establish shared priorities and performance measures, and nurture a team approach among these units in support of university-wide economic development goals. Communications Role With the VPR , the AVP communicates within the university about economic development initiatives, opportunities, and outcomes and works with communications teams to advance this priority. The AVP will: Partner with university communications teams to develop compelling narratives, case studies, briefing materials, presentations, and reports that demonstrate the impact of UVM partnerships and innovation activity and support efforts to attract additional partners and investment. Provide timely strategic advice, investment recommendations, and concise decision materials to the VPR and other UVM leaders. Represent the VPR and the university on committees, councils, working groups, and external forums relevant to economic development, innovation, industry engagement, and entrepreneurship. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Master’s degree and significant progressively responsible leadership experience in economic development, innovation, industry engagement, entrepreneurship, technology commercialization, and/or corporate philanthropy, or a related field. Demonstrated success developing and executing complex initiatives from concept through launch, including securing resources and coordinating multiple internal and external stakeholders and producing measurable outcomes. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with and influence senior leaders and partners across academic, corporate, government, nonprofit, and community settings, including in a decentralized organizational environment. Desirable Qualifications Experience in a research university, public research organization, economic development agency, innovation district, technology-based enterprise, or comparable innovation or partnership environment. Experience designing and launching multi-partner economic development initiatives, structuring public-private partnerships, or advancing industry-institutional partnerships. Experience developing performance indicators, using them to assess progress and inform decisions, and communicating economic, research, workforce, or community impact. Knowledge of Vermont’s or a comparable state or regional innovation and economic development ecosystem. Anticipated Pay Range $190,000 - $225,000 Other Information Special Conditions Non-standard work hours required, A probationary period may be required, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), Travel to and from worksites required, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position No Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 09/21/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Research Commercialztn MG5 X Posting Number S6308PO Department VP Research Admin Office/30600 Position Number 00028003 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
