      "title": "Artificial Intelligence and Modern Work Specialist",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Artificial Intelligence and Modern Work Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Artificial Intelligence and Modern Work Specialist Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Artificial Intelligence and Modern Work Specialist Posting Summary The Artificial Intelligence and Modern Work Specialist will focus and specialize on implementation and technical consulting for Artificial Intelligence and Modern Work solutions. As a member of the SAA Collaboration Services team, provide university-wide consulting about emerging technologies such as Artificial Intelligence tools and help build Al services and solutions to address campus needs. Support modern work solutions at UVM , providing guidance and training for services such as the Microsoft 365 platform and helping departments with expert guidance for tools such as Power Automate to support low-code workflow solutions, bringing processes improvements across UVM . Enable and promote enhanced consulting, structured end-user training, departmental engagement, and proactive adoption programs for Microsoft 365, Copilot, and adjacent technologies, with the goal of lifting organization-wide productivity through wider and deeper adoption of modern work practices and collaboration tools and services. Assist departments and employees to make more effective use of Al and modern work tools in secured UVM managed environments, prioritizing data security and privacy. Contribute to maximizing the value of UVM’s licensing investments by providing training and consulting for both Al and our Microsoft 365 environment. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor’s degree in technology related field and five years of relevant experience. Four additional years of experience can substitute for the degree. Excellent written and verbal communication, documentation skills, and experience public speaking and delivering trainings. Experience with Generative AI systems like Copilot and ChatGPT, including experience building agents and chatbots. Effective troubleshooting skills, including system and network diagnostic experience. Excellent customer service experience. Desirable Qualifications Experience with Power Platform tools such as Power Automate and Power BI. Proficiency with Windows scripting and automation tools, ideally PowerShell. Experience with Microsoft 365 services administration. Experience with Active Directory and Group Policy. Expertise with Exchange, SharePoint, traditional file and print services, or related technologies. Experience working at an academic institution. Anticipated Pay Range 70,000-82,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 08/26/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Technology Generalist PC2 X Posting Number S6274PO Department Systems Architecture & Admin/11620 Position Number 00027749 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The Universit